**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** The kit bar above the workbench: the kit, the Kit menu, the constructor and its switch, the reload offer and the kit status, in a file of its own (001 §O 'Kit menu: Send kit…, Show in Explorer, Copy experiments from another kit…, Reload changes, Close kit', of which S6 adds Send kit… and Copy experiments…; .spec-md §4: new surfaces live in their own files, and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` hosts them through messages; §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; AGENTS.md: never a wrapping `TextBlock` inside a horizontal `StackPanel`). The Kit menu is the bar's verb row, not an Avalonia `Menu`: a popup is not provable headless, which is why the element menu is a model-driven overlay (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:117`), and the ribbon's bay order is fixed (Add first, Details last, spec 0046). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the start-screen group (step 178), `// --- The kit window's kit bar (KitWindowView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `kitBar` (`"KitBar"`), `kitCaptionText` (`"KitCaptionText"`), `kitShowInExplorerButton` (`"KitShowInExplorerButton"`), `kitReloadChangesButton` (`"KitReloadChangesButton"`), `kitCloseButton` (`"KitCloseButton"`), `kitModeText` (`"KitModeText"`), `kitSwitchModeButton` (`"KitSwitchModeButton"`), `kitChangesText` (`"KitChangesText"`), `kitChangesReloadButton` (`"KitChangesReloadButton"`) and `kitChangesKeepMineButton` (`"KitChangesKeepMineButton"`); the doc of `kitStatus` (step 152) says it is the kit bar's status line. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView`, compiled directly after `KitStartView.fs` (step 176): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3. `kitWindowView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel` whose top child is the kit bar and whose fill is `mainView model dispatch` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3938`), so the bar stays in view while the page scrolls. The bar is one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitBar`, margin 8, 6, 8, 2, holding in order: (a) a `DockPanel` whose left child is the semi-bold `TextBlock` `Kit:` and whose fill is a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitCaptionText` with `model.kitCaption` (step 184); (b) a `WrapPanel` holding the Kit menu's verbs, each a `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (public since step 107): `Show in Explorer` (`kitShowInExplorerButton`, sending `ShowKitInExplorer`, present only when `kitFolderOpt` is `Some`), `Reload changes` (`kitReloadChangesButton`, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnRequest`) and `Close kit` (`kitCloseButton`, `CloseKit`), then a `TextBlock` carrying `kitModeText` reading `Main constructor` or `Inverse constructor`, and the verb `kitSwitchModeButton` labelled `Switch to Inverse` in the forward constructor (sending `SwitchConstructorMode InverseConstructor`) and `Switch to Main` in the inverse one (sending `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor`); (c) when `kitChanges` is not empty, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitChangesText`, `Changed outside the app: <the file names joined by ", ">. Reload them, or keep your version?`, and under it one horizontal `StackPanel` of two `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton`s: `Reload` (`kitChangesReloadButton`, `positiveBackground`, `ReloadKitChanges`) and `Keep mine` (`kitChangesKeepMineButton`, `negativeBackground`, `KeepMyKitChanges`), the action box's right margin being the gap; (d) when `kitStatus` is `Some`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitStatus` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`. Every id is an AutomationId, never a `Name`, as `MaterialsWindowView.fs:verbButton`'s doc says of variable membership. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `collectionBuilderView` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3484`) no longer shows the `kitStatus` line (step 152), because the kit bar shows it whichever bay is open, and one control carries the id; its doc and the section comment say so. (4) Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184) mounts its screens as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts a view (`:107`), over `kitWindowView`, headless at 1000 × 700, each model loaded from a folder kit with a recording `kitShell` (step 186). Without a trait: `the kit window UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the ten new ids' texts. `the kit bar shows the kit, its Kit menu and the constructor`: `kitCaptionText` reads the model's `kitCaption`; `kitShowInExplorerButton`, `kitReloadChangesButton` and `kitCloseButton` are present; `kitModeText` reads `Main constructor` and `kitSwitchModeButton` `Switch to Inverse`, and over the inverse model `Inverse constructor` and `Switch to Main`; over `initMain ()`, the scratch kit, `kitShowInExplorerButton` is absent. `a changed kit offers Reload and Keep mine on one row, Keep mine to the right`: over a model whose `kitChanges` holds `.kit-json` and `E2.experiment-json`, `kitChangesText` names both, and the two buttons have equal tops, `kitChangesKeepMineButton`'s left beyond `kitChangesReloadButton`'s right; with no changes neither button exists. `the kit status shows in the kit bar whichever bay is open`: a model whose `kitStatus` is `Some` shows exactly one control carrying `kitStatus`, with the Add bay open and with the Experiments bay open. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does (`:69`): `pressing the kit bar's buttons sends their messages`: `kitSwitchModeButton` switches the model to the inverse constructor (`kitModeText` then reads `Inverse constructor`), `kitShowInExplorerButton` hands the kit's folder to the recording explorer, `kitReloadChangesButton` shows `No kit file changed outside the app.` in `kitStatus`, and `kitCloseButton` asks the recording close once. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`: `assertReachable "KitWindow"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over `filledExperiments ()` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:114`) updated, as a record, to a kit marked `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, a test-local `kitFolderOpt`, three file names in `kitChanges` and a `kitStatus`, so the bar is at its tallest. `InverseConstructorTests`' and `SceneSaveLoadTests`' facts keep their assertions: they read `kitStatus` from the model, and the builder still renders.

**Acceptance.** After the kit bar lands, `kitWindowView` MUST show above `mainView` the kit's caption, the Kit menu (Show in Explorer, Reload changes, Close kit), the constructor with its switch, the reload offer with Reload and Keep mine on one row and the kit status, every control under its `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing the kit bar's buttons sends their messages`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit window UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the kit bar shows the kit, its Kit menu and the constructor`, `a changed kit offers Reload and Keep mine on one row, Keep mine to the right`, `the kit status shows in the kit bar whichever bay is open` and `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
